      "kind": "lede",
      "html": "<p>Temperature control is one of the most checked things in a UK kitchen. It is also easy to fill in afterwards. Fridges at open and close. Cooking probes. Hot holding. Cool-down at night. Together they are the temperature record an inspector may ask to see. So the question is whether the reading is logged when the probe comes out, or written up after close from memory.</p>"
