      "html": "<p><strong>Fridges and freezers.</strong> Log each unit at open and close, or more often if it is unreliable. A drifting fridge caught in the morning is a repair. Caught at close it is a bin.</p><p><strong>Cooking.</strong> Probe the core of cooked dishes, especially high-risk ones. Log the reading against the dish.</p><p><strong>Hot holding.</strong> Check hot food stays at or above 63C unless it is served straight away.</p><p><strong>Cool-down.</strong> Record that cooked food was cooled fast and chilled. </p>"
