      "html": "<h3>What temperature should a commercial fridge be in the UK?</h3><p>In England, Wales and Northern Ireland the law says chilled food must be kept at or below 8C, and in Scotland that is recommended. The FSA advises setting fridges to 5C or below. Many kitchens run fridges colder, often 1C to 4C, so a small drift does not break the limit. Check current FSA guidance and the HACCP plan. This is not legal advice.</p><h3>What core temperature should food be cooked to?</h3><p>FSA standard advice is 70C for two minutes, or an equal time and temperature, such as 75C for 30 seconds or 80C for six seconds. Hot food must be kept at or above 63C if it is not served straight away. Follow current FSA guidance.</p><h3>Can I log kitchen temperatures in WhatsApp?</h3><p>Yes. Each check arrives as a message. You reply with the reading, a voice note or a photo of the probe. The log is written for you with the time. A reading that is out of limit is flagged at once.</p><h3>Does a log app replace a probe thermometer?</h3><p>No. Quickler records the reading you take with your own calibrated probe or fridge thermometer. It adds the time and, if useful, a photo. It does not measure anything and does not keep the fridge cold.</p><h3>Related guides</h3><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/food-safety-audit-app-uk.html\">Food safety audit app</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/haccp-checklist-app-uk.html\">HACCP checklist app</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/due-diligence-food-hygiene-uk.html\">Food hygiene due diligence records</a></li></ul>"
